  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bf402000706b3fe42b429548fcf1d4fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: Duelist(Huskybaseclass)
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::_Scripts.Runtime.Characters.Classes.Scripts.CombatClassSO
  defaultAttackElements: 
  _className: 
  _defaultAttackRange: 0
  _classDescription: 'Description: A close range physical fighter who switches between
    attacking and defensive stances, depending on whether they want to keep up the
    assault or prepare for incoming hits while still having the opportunity to dish
    out damage.'
  effects:
  - 'Gain a strength percentage boost per enemy currently applied with Hunt, Tier
    1 (Moderate): 20%, Tier 2 (High): 40%, Tier 3 (Extreme): 60%.'
  - 'Defending Overclock

    Effect:Gain a starting 50% chance, increasing with
    25% per tier to fully negate oncoming damage, and empowering the next counter
    by the chance percentage if an attack was successfully negated.(Essentially a
    parry.)'
  explanations:
  - "Pretty self explanatory, if there\u2019s 3 enemies let\u2019s say currently
    with the Hunt debuff, then at a moderate overclock tier, duelist would get a
    60% strength buff (was thinking about doing individual stacks at first, but I
    feel just counting the enemies would be smoother.) This would encourage spreading
    hunt as much as possible, and set up a massive attack buff with the other effects
    in mind."
  - "Explanation:Example, after overclocking once and doing defend as an action,
    there would be a 50% chance when getting hit to fully negate that damage, and
    increase the incoming counter percent based damage by 50%. Otherwise, if an attack
    wasn\u2019t negated, counter would still apply normally."
